From: haidoan2098
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: am335x-boneblack: disable cape EEPROMs and eMMC

No cape is used on this board; do not probe the four cape ID EEPROMs
on i2c2. The i2c2 bus itself stays enabled.

The on-board eMMC is not used yet: boot and rootfs are on the SD card.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [boot time study, board specific]
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-boneblack.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-boneblack.dts
@@ -178,3 +178,28 @@
 &baseboard_eeprom {
 	vcc-supply = <&ldo4_reg>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * No BeagleBone cape is used: do not probe the cape ID EEPROMs on i2c2.
+ * The i2c2 bus itself stays enabled for future devices.
+ */
+&cape_eeprom0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&cape_eeprom1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&cape_eeprom2 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&cape_eeprom3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/* The on-board eMMC is not used yet (boot and rootfs are on the SD card). */
+&mmc2 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
